What is SSH?
SSH allows secure remote access to Linux servers.

Connect Server
ssh ec2-user@10.0.0.10

Generate SSH Key
ssh-keygen

Output:

id_rsa
id_rsa.pub
Copy Public Key
ssh-copy-id ec2-user@10.0.0.10
Passwordless Login
ssh ec2-user@10.0.0.10

No password required.

Run Remote Command
ssh ec2-user@10.0.0.10 "uptime"
Real-Time DevOps Example

Check Multiple Servers

#!/bin/bash

for SERVER in $(cat servers.txt)
do
    ssh ec2-user@$SERVER "df -h"
done
